/*
  The opening scene. The detective walks the crime scene and LOGS evidence:
  each `::assert{ foundClue(...) }` writes a relational-fact delta (0.3.0 §5),
  and each `::set{ run.cluesLogged += 1 }` bumps the scalar counter the quest's
  `gatherEvidence` objective gates on. Both asserts run on the only route
  through the scene, so `check-project` knows `foundClue(ledger)`,
  `foundClue(letter)`, and the derived `points(blake)` hold in every scene
  sequenced `after:` this one (dsl 0.20.0 fact envelopes).
*/

## The Study

@narrator: The victim's study, untouched since the coroner left.
@detective{mono}: Two things in here don't belong. Log them.

::assert{ foundClue(ledger) }
::set{ run.cluesLogged += 1 }
@detective: A ledger — the balances scratched out in red ink.

::assert{ foundClue(letter) }
::set{ run.cluesLogged += 1 }
@detective: And a letter, signed once and then unsigned.

/*
  No `when=` here. A guard `holds(points(blake))` over the DERIVED relation
  `points` (0.3.0 §7) would be redundant: both clues above are asserted on the
  only route through this shot, and `implicates(ledger, blake)` is seeded, so
  the rule derives `points(blake)` before this line on every playthrough.
  `check-project` proves that and reports such a guard as `W-FACT-GUARANTEED`
  (dsl 0.20.0 §5).
*/
@detective{mono}: Both threads pull toward one name.
